  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **The Dump**: rare: 8 archived performances [3]\n- **unknown &gt**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2003-08-30.schoeps.ackerman.flac24** (recommended): source not stated; 9 songs; 106 min [1]\n- **soulive2003-08-30.kreider.skm140**: audience recording; 8 songs; 108 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The show took place at the Arts Quad of Cornell University in Ithaca, NY [1]\n- The performance was held at the Arts Quad at Cornell University in Ithaca, NY [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2003-08-30.schoeps.ackerman.flac24**: taped by Ray Ackerman; transferred by Ray Ackerman / Dave Mallick; source: Schoeps CCM4s > Lunatec V3 > Sony D-10 Pro II (on stage) [1]. Also: Recorded on-stage with Schoeps CCM4 microphones into a Lunatec V3 preamp and a Sony D-10 Pro II recorder; Transfer went through Sound Studio 4.11.0 and xACT 2.58, ending as FLAC files [1]\n- **soulive2003-08-30.kreider.skm140**: taped by Keith Kreider; transferred by Keith; source: AUD:DAT [2]. Also: Recorded with Neumann SKM-140 mics in ORTF configuration, placed 10 feet from the front of the board and 15 feet from the roof; Transferred from a Sony DTC-790 via Zoltrix Nightingale Pro 6 optical into Sound Forge 6.0, then SHN to FLAC; recorded and mastered by Keith Kreider [2]",
